WEBVTT

00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:04.802
PyTorch gives us the complete multi-head attention operation in one layer.

00:00:04.802 --> 00:00:10.687
We create nn.MultiheadAttention with an embedding dimension and a number of heads.

00:00:10.687 --> 00:00:17.942
With batch_first set to True, the expected tensor shape is batch, sequence length, hidden dimension,

00:00:17.942 --> 00:00:20.242
which is often easier to read.

00:00:20.242 --> 00:00:25.487
In self-attention, we call the layer with x as Query, Key, and Value.

00:00:25.487 --> 00:00:30.022
The layer returns two useful objects.

00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:33.947
attention_output contains the updated token vectors.

00:00:33.947 --> 00:00:35.947
attention_weights contains the learned weighting pattern,

00:00:35.947 --> 00:00:40.487
usually averaged across heads unless we request per-head weights.

00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:47.662
Try printing both shapes before worrying about the actual numbers.

00:00:47.662 --> 00:00:51.907
Shape tracking is one of the best habits in deep-learning code.

00:00:51.907 --> 00:00:56.682
If x begins as batch size two, sequence length five, hidden size eight,

00:00:56.682 --> 00:01:02.352
the attention output should remain compatible with that hidden size.

00:01:02.352 --> 00:01:06.078
That compatibility is what allows the next residual connection.
